From: surface-kit
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: af: refocus when an app touches a trigger file

Apps show the camera through PipeWire, which doesn't pass
controls::AfTrigger on, so a "focus again" button or a tap on the picture
had no way to reach the autofocus. Af now watches the time stamp of
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/libcamera-af-trigger (one stat() every 5 frames) and
starts a full sweep when it changes; the stamp at configure() is taken as
seen, so a stale file does nothing. GNOME Camera (surface-kit patch)
writes it. Measured: sweep starts within 0.25 s, focused ~1.4 s later.

---
